PART 3: THIRD-PARTY OBSERVATIONAL DATA ATTRIBUTION (`cufg/data/`)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The observational astronomy tables and FITS profiles stored in `cufg/data/` are
publicly released scientific datasets produced by external research groups.
They are included solely for offline reproducibility of the benchmark suite and
remain the intellectual work of their respective authors, to whom all credit
and citations belong:

1. SPARC (Spitzer Photometry and Accurate Rotation Curves) Database
   - Files: `cufg/data/sparc_table1_galaxies.csv`, `cufg/data/sparc_table2_massmodels.csv`
   - Authors & Credit: Federico Lelli, Stacy S. McGaugh, and James M. Schombert
   - Primary Citations:
     * Lelli, F., McGaugh, S. S., & Schombert, J. M. (2016), "SPARC: Mass Models
       for 175 Disk Galaxies with Spitzer Photometry and Accurate Rotation Curves,"
       The Astronomical Journal, 152, 157 (doi:10.3847/0004-6256/152/6/157;
       arXiv:1606.09251).
     * McGaugh, S. S., Lelli, F., & Schombert, J. M. (2016), "Radial Acceleration
       Relation in Rotationally Supported Galaxies," Physical Review Letters,
       117, 201101 (doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.117.201101; arXiv:1609.05917).
   - Source Archive: CDS VizieR Catalog J/AJ/152/157
     (https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/J/AJ/152/157) and the SPARC
     Project Archive (http://astroweb.cwru.edu/SPARC/).

2. X-COP (XMM-Newton Cluster Outskirts Project) Galaxy Cluster Data Products
   - Files: `cufg/data/xcop_fits/*.fits`, `cufg/data/xcop_12clusters_radial_profiles.csv`,
     `cufg/data/xcop_ettori2019_table1.csv`, `cufg/data/xcop_eckert2019_table2.csv`
   - Authors & Credit: The X-COP Collaboration (Dominique Eckert, Stefano Ettori,
     Vittorio Ghirardini, et al.)
   - Primary Citations:
     * Ettori, S., Ghirardini, V., Eckert, D., Pointecouteau, E., Gastaldello, F.,
       Sereno, M., Gaspari, M., Ghizzardi, S., Bourdin, H., & Rossetti, M. (2019),
       "Hydrostatic mass profiles in X-COP galaxy clusters," Astronomy & Astrophysics,
       621, A39 (doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201833323; arXiv:1805.00035).
     * Eckert, D., Ghirardini, V., Ettori, S., Rasia, E., Biffi, V., Pointecouteau, E.,
       Rossetti, M., Molendi, S., Vazza, F., Gastaldello, F., Gaspari, M., De Grandi, S.,
       Ghizzardi, S., Bourdin, H., Tchernin, C., & Roncarelli, M. (2019),
       "Non-thermal pressure support in X-COP galaxy clusters," Astronomy & Astrophysics,
       621, A40 (doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201833324; arXiv:1805.00034).
     * Ghirardini, V., Eckert, D., Ettori, S., et al. (2019), "Universal thermodynamic
       properties of the intracluster medium over two decades in radius in the X-COP
       sample," Astronomy & Astrophysics, 621, A41 (doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201833325).
   - Source Archive: University of Geneva X-COP Public Data Release
     (https://dominiqueeckert.wixsite.com/xcop/data-products) and arXiv source
     packages arXiv:1805.00034 / arXiv:1805.00035.
